  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome (100% probability) in either lottery and prefers the one without such a sure outcome. However, in this case, neither lottery has a sure outcome, so the reason would not lead to a preference for either. The individual, in contrast, based their decision on the higher potential gain in A and the small difference in probabilities, showing a sensitivity to magnitude and near-equality in chances. There is no evidence in the verbal report that the individual considered whether an outcome was certain or not. The information used by the individual (maximum payoff, similarity in probabilities) does not overlap with the information required by the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome). Furthermore, the justification is based on outcome magnitude and probability comparison, not on avoidance of sure outcomes. Therefore, there is no indication that the decision reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
